  "regressions": 4,
  "scope": "Whole five-part Federer 3.2.28, pp. 263\u2013267: actual smooth Stiefel and oriented/unoriented Grassmann manifolds, symmetric dimension and exact Gram-kernel tangents; arbitrary-unit top-exterior Hom evaluation isometry; actual exterior and forgetful differentials, full adapted bases, exact tangent partial Jacobians and finite horizontal determinant increment; actual SO and spherical fibres, all actual coarea volume identities; the unrestricted square-map manifold and twofold area assertions, including noncompact manifolds and infinite mass; both exact printed Euler Gamma volume formulas, and positive atomic/empty-product boundaries.",
  "proof_route": "Specify finite orthonormal ambient charts, complements, frame extensions and Grassmann squares independently and prove local existence. The actual symmetric Gram field gives regular smooth fibres and tangents. Exterior-word calculus, horizontal/vertical decomposition and actual orthonormal rectangular exterior norms give the computed Jacobians without auxiliary frame or Jacobian premises. Homogeneous orbit laws give openness, independently of compactness. Prove compactness, measurability, finite rectifiability, Lipschitz bounds and actual approximate-Jacobian transport, then apply 3.2.22 with actual constant fibre integrals. For the square map, compute the actual symmetric differential, metric/fibre identities and smooth image charts; prove the actual Jacobian on compact rectifiable subsets and apply 3.2.20. An increasing antipodal compact exhaustion and measure continuity below give the full noncompact manifold area assertion. The actual sphere Gamma mass and coarea recurrence, with locally existing orthogonal restrictions and an empty-frame base, prove the exact real-power Stiefel scalar; positive finite scalar cancellation and actual twofold area give the Grassmann formula.",
  "erratum_and_conventions": "Apply erratum p. 5, book p. 265 line 3 (delete the compactness phrase in the openness argument) and line 12 (alpha belongs to O(m,m-1)). Positive m is required for Grassmann orientations and SO half-volume; the Stiefel recurrence and Gamma formula extend to the unique empty frame of H^0 mass one. The Grassmann numerator Gamma product is indexed in reverse order.",
